contractRequests:
07 section 9 item 21, work bound: record the uniqueItems comparison charges. The library's hash keeps neither number signs nor the bounds of nested values, so:
- array and object items are charged comparisons with every other item;
- decimals get at most 2(L+3) comparisons per item, L being the literal's byte bound;
- strings, booleans, nulls and integers get one comparison per item.
Consequence: at the 10 MiB default, a valid uniqueItems array of more than a few thousand objects is 413. A possible refinement is exact hash classes at scan time.
